1
00:00:00,460 --> 00:00:06,150
January eleventh, 2020. Scientists post
the new coronavirus's genome online,

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,830
for anyone to use.

3
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:13,230
Sixty-five days later, the first
volunteer in a vaccine trial gets a dose.

4
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:18,184
In July, large trials begin, each planned
for about thirty thousand volunteers.

5
00:00:18,514 --> 00:00:22,464
December second, the UK
authorises the first vaccine.

6
00:00:22,514 --> 00:00:25,704
December eighth, at 6:31 in
the morning, Margaret Keenan,

7
00:00:25,754 --> 00:00:29,647
ninety, gets the first
authorised dose outside a trial.

8
00:00:30,027 --> 00:00:33,746
Three hundred and thirty-two
days, end to end, on one line.

9
00:00:36,987 --> 00:00:40,369
That's OpenChronology. It's free.
